  <section class="process wrap" id="process" aria-labelledby="proc-h">
    <h2 id="proc-h" class="h-head">From consultation to long-term output</h2>
    <div class="steps">
      <article class="step"><figure><img src="/images/b2b/step-design.webp" alt="Engineering drawings on a desk" loading="lazy" width="1067" height="1600"></figure><h3>Consultation</h3><p>Share your electricity bill and goals. We recommend the scheme that fits your load profile.</p></article>
      <article class="step"><figure><img src="/images/b2b/step-feasibility.webp" alt="Engineer surveying a factory roof" loading="lazy" width="1067" height="1600"></figure><h3>Site survey and design</h3><p>Roof survey, load profile and sizing, with string and micro inverters matched to the roof.</p></article>
      <article class="step"><figure><img src="/images/b2b/step-approvals.webp" alt="Engineer testing a main switchboard" loading="lazy" width="1067" height="1600"></figure><h3>Proposal and contract</h3><p>A clear proposal with milestone-based payments, financing options and GITA incentives.</p></article>
      <article class="step"><figure><img src="/images/b2b/step-commissioning.webp" alt="Engineer inspecting string inverters" loading="lazy" width="1067" height="1600"></figure><h3>Approvals</h3><p>We prepare and submit SEDA and utility applications. Regulator timelines apply.</p></article>
      <article class="step"><figure><img src="/images/b2b/step-construction.webp" alt="Crane lifting solar modules onto a factory roof" loading="lazy" width="1067" height="1600"></figure><h3>Installation and commissioning</h3><p>Certified crews with site supervision. Most C&amp;I rooftops take 4 to 8 weeks from survey to commissioning.</p></article>
      <article class="step"><figure><img src="/images/b2b/real/thermal-drone-scan.webp" alt="Thermal and visual drone images of the same solar roof" loading="lazy" width="1500" height="598"></figure><h3>Monitoring and maintenance</h3><p>eSAJ real-time data, inspection every six months and thermal drone scans, backed by our hotline.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

